# Behind the store of null the local variable may hold the only reference to the follower, and the call allocates, so it may collect. The read stays in front of the store,
# and the word that was read is the one that is tested and read from behind the call: it is neither read again nor made again from anything else.
# CHECK-LABEL: name="weigh" role=Source
# CHECK-NEXT: BB#0:
# CHECK: Int64 b@[[follower]] = Load(b@[[entry]], offset = 16, ControlDependent|Reads:ObjectFields{{*}}:GetSlot)
# CHECK: Store($2(b@{{*}}), b@[[entry]], offset = 16, ControlDependent|Writes:ObjectFields{{*}}:PutSlot)
# CHECK: Patchpoint(b@{{*}}:Register({{*}}), resultConstraints = WarmAny, ControlDependent|Writes:{collectorState, {{*}}:CallDirect)
# CHECK-NEXT: Int32 b@[[isNull]] = Equal(b@[[follower]], $2(b@{{*}}), {{*}}:TypeTest)
# CHECK-NEXT: Branch(b@[[isNull]], Terminal, {{*}}:TypeTest)
# CHECK: Double b@{{*}} = Load(b@[[follower]], offset = 24, ControlDependent|Reads:ObjectFields{{*}}:GetSlot)
# CHECK-LABEL: end of function
# Across the call the whole word lies in a register that every callee saves into its own frame before it uses it, which is where the collector looks.
# X64-LABEL: name="weigh" role=Source
# X64-NEXT: BB#0:
# X64-NEXT: EnterFrame $0, %rbx
# X64-NEXT: Move 16(%rdi), %rbx
# X64: Patch &Patchpoint
# X64-NEXT: Branch64 Equal, %rbx, $2
# X64: MoveDouble 24(%rbx), %xmm0
# X64-LABEL: end of function
# ARM64-LABEL: name="weigh" role=Source
# ARM64-NEXT: BB#0:
# ARM64-NEXT: EnterFrame {{*}}, %x19
# ARM64-NEXT: Move 16(%x0), %x19
# ARM64: Patch &Patchpoint
# ARM64-NEXT: Branch64 Equal, %x19, $2
# ARM64: MoveDouble 24(%x19), %q0
# ARM64-LABEL: end of function
